    "created_at": "2021-09-06T19:07:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-06T19:07:57Z",
    "body": "Thanks for opening this! I've had a similar idea brewing in the back of my mind for a little bit, but I didn't have a great feel for how people would prefer to see it implemented.\r\n\r\nI'd be slightly concerned about distributing TOML files with the project since this would represent a packaging change, and we have a lot of different packages out there, not all of which are under our direct control.\r\n\r\nWe currently implement a single default set of configs for starship in the binary and allow the user to print the corresponding config with the `print-config` command. If we were to implement multiple presets within the starship binary and allow you to select between them in the manner you describe, as well as hooking them in to the `print-config` mechanism, would this cover all your use cases?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
